G1438.def:
**ἑαυτοῦ**, -ῆς, -οῦ, dative -ῷ, etc., accusative -όν, etc., pi. -ῶν, etc. (Att. contr. αὑτοῦ, etc);
_reflex pron._;
1. prop, of 3rd person (Lat. sui, sibi, se), **of himself, herself, itself**, etc.: [[Mat.27.42|Mat.27:42]], [[Mrk.15.31|Mrk.15:31]], [[Luk.23.35|Luk.23:35]], al.; added to a middle verb, διεμερίσαντο ἑαυτοῖς, [[Jhn.19.24|Jhn.19:24]] to an active verb, [[Act.14.14|Act.14:14]] (M, _Pr._, 157); ἀφ᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, [[Luk.12.57; 21.30|Luk.12:57 21:30]], [[Jhn.5.19|Jhn.5:19]], al. (see: ἀπό); δι᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, [[Rom.14.14|Rom.14:14]] ἐν ἑ., [[Mat.3.9|Mat.3:9]], [[Mrk.5.30|Mrk.5:30]], al.; εἰς ἑ., [[Luk.15.17|Luk.15:17]] καθ᾽ ἑαυτόν, [[Act.28.16|Act.28:16]], [[Jas.2.17|Jas.2:17]]; παρ᾽ ἑαυτῷ, **at his own house**, [[1Co.16.2|1Co.16:2]] πρὸς ἑ., **with, to himself**, [[Luk.18.11|Luk.18:11]] as poss. pron. (with emphasis weakened; see M, _Pr._, 87f.), τ. ἑαυτῶν νεκρούς, [[Luk.9.60|Luk.9:60]]
2. As reflexive 1st and 2nd of person(s) (so also frequently in cl., chiefly poetry), [[Mat.23.31|Mat.23:31]], [[Mrk.9.50|Mrk.9:50]], [[Rom.8.23|Rom.8:23]], [[1Th.2.8|1Th.2:8]], al.
3. In pl., for reciprocal pron., ἀλλήλων, -οις, -ους, **of one another**, etc.: [[Mat.21.38|Mat.21:38]], [[Mrk.16.3|Mrk.16:3]], [[Eph.5.19|Eph.5:19]], al.
(AS)

G1437.def:
**ἐάν**, contr. fr. εἰ ἄν,
_conditional particle_,
representing something as "under certain circumstances actual or liable to happen," but not so definitely expected as in the case of εἰ with ind. (Bl., §65, 4; cf. [[Jhn.13.17|Jhn.13:17]], [[1Co.7.36|1Co.7:36]]), **if haply, if**;
1. with subjc. (cl.);
(a) pres.: [[Mat.6.22|Mat.6:22]], [[Luk.10.6|Luk.10:6]], [[Jhn.7.17|Jhn.7:17]], [[Rom.2.25, 26|Rom.2:25, 26]] al.;
{ (b) aor. (= Lat. fut. pf.): [[Mat.4.9; 16.26|Mat.4:9 16:26]] (cf. ptcp. in [[Luk.9.25|Luk.9:25]] M, _Pr._, 230), [[Mrk.3.24|Mrk.3:24]], [[Luk.14.34|Luk.14:34]], [[Jhn.5.43|Jhn.5:43]], [[Rom.7.2|Rom.7:2]], al.; = cl. εἰ, with opt., [[Jhn.9.22; 11.57|Jhn.9:22 11:57]], [[Act.9.2|Act.9:2]]; as Heb. אִם = ὅταν, [[Jhn.12.32; 14.3|Jhn.12:32 14:3]], I [[Jhn.2.28; 3.2|Jhn.2:28 3:2]], [[Heb.3.7|Heb.3:7]]" (LXX) .
2. C. indic, (as in late writers, fr. Arist. on; see WH, _App._, 171; VD, _MGr._ 2, _App._, §77; Deiss., _BS_, 201f., _LAE_, 155, 254; M, _Pr._, 168, 187; Bl., §65, 4);
(a) fut.: [[Mat.18.19|Mat.18:19]] T, [[Luk.19.40|Luk.19:40]], [[Act.7.7|Act.7:7]]
(b) pres.: [[1Th.3.8|1Th.3:8]] (see Milligan, in l.).
3. **With other particles**: ἐ. καί (Bl., §65, 6), [[Gal.6.1|Gal.6:1]] ἐ. μή (M, _Pr._, 185, 187; Bl., l.with), with subjc. pres., [[Mat.10.13|Mat.10:13]], [[1Co.8.8|1Co.8:8]], [[Jas.2.17|Jas.2:17]], [[1Jn.3.21|1Jn.3:21]] aor., [[Mat.6.15|Mat.6:15]], [[Mrk.3.27|Mrk.3:27]], [[Jhn.3.3|Jhn.3:3]], [[Rom.10.15|Rom.10:15]], [[Gal.1.8; 2.16|Gal.1:8 2:16]] (see Lft., Ellic., in ll.); ἐ. τε . . . ἐ. τε, [in LXX for אִם . . . אִם, [[Est.19.13|Est.19:13]], al.,] [[Rom.14.8|Rom.14:8]].
4. = cl. ἄν (which see) after relat. pronouns and adverbs (Tdf., _Pr._, 96; WH, _App._, 173; M, _Pr._, 42f.; Bl., §26, 4; Mayser, 152f.; Deiss., _BS_, 202ff.): ὃς ἐ., [[Mat.5.19|Mat.5:19]], [[Mrk.6.22, 23|Mrk.6:22, 23]] [[Luk.17.32|Luk.17:32]], [[1Co.6.18|1Co.6:18]], al.; ὅπου ἐ., [[Mat.8.19|Mat.8:19]] ὁσάκις ἐ., [[Rev.11.6|Rev.11:6]] οὗ ἐ., [[1Co.16.6|1Co.16:6]] καθὸ ἐ., [[2Co.8.12|2Co.8:12]] ὅστις ἐ., [[Gal.5.10|Gal.5:10]]
(AS)

G1411.def:
**δύναμις**, -εως, ἡ
(δύναμαι), [in LXX for עֹז ,גּבוּרָה ,צָבָה ,(חֵיל) חַיִל, etc.; 35 words in all ;]
**power, might, strength**; relatively, **ability, power** to perform: [[Mat.25.15|Mat.25:15]], [[Act.3.12|Act.3:12]], [[Heb.11.11|Heb.11:11]]; κατὰ δ., [[2Co.8.3|2Co.8:3]] παρὰ δ., ib.; ὑπὲρ δ., [[2Co.1.8|2Co.1:8]] of pecuniary ability, [[2Co.8.3|2Co.8:3]], [[Rev.18.3|Rev.18:3]]; absol., **power, might**: [[Luk.24.49|Luk.24:49]], [[Act.1.8|Act.1:8]]; opposite to ἀσθένεια, [[1Co.15.43|1Co.15:43]] ἡ δ. τ. ἁμαρτίας, [[1Co.15.56|1Co.15:56]] of power in action, [[Rom.1.16, 20|Rom.1:16, 20]] [[1Co.1.18|1Co.1:18]], [[Php.3.10|Php.3:10]], al.; ἡ δ. τ. θεοῦ, [[Mat.22.29|Mat.22:29]], [[Mrk.12.24|Mrk.12:24]], [[Rom.1.20|Rom.1:20]], al.; opposite to μόρφωσις, [[2Ti.3.5|2Ti.3:5]] in doxologies, [[Rev.4.11; 7.12|Rev.4:11 7:12]], al.; ἐν δ., [[Mrk.9.1|Mrk.9:1]], [[Luk.4.36|Luk.4:36]], [[Rom.1.4|Rom.1:4]], al.; of the power of performing miracles, [[Act.6.8|Act.6:8]], [[2Th.2.9|2Th.2:9]]; pl., [[Mat.13.54|Mat.13:54]], [[Mrk.6.14|Mrk.6:14]], [[Gal.3.5|Gal.3:5]], al.; of the **force** or **meaning** of a word (Plat., al.), [[1Co.14.11|1Co.14:11]] By meton., of persons or things;
(a) of God, [[Mat.26.64|Mat.26:64]], [[Mrk.14.62|Mrk.14:62]] (Dalman, _Words_, 200ff.);
(b) of angels, [[Rom.8.38|Rom.8:38]], [[Eph.1.21|Eph.1:21]], [[1Pe.3.22|1Pe.3:22]];
(with) of armies, pl. [LXX for צְבָאוֹת ], metaphorically, of the stars, [[Mat.24.29|Mat.24:29]], [[Mrk.13.25|Mrk.13:25]], [[Luk.21.26|Luk.21:26]];
(d) of that wh. manifests God's power: Christ, [[1Co.1.24|1Co.1:24]] τ. εὐαγγέλλιον, [[Rom.1.16|Rom.1:16]] ἡ δ. τ. κυρίου, [[1Co.5.4|1Co.5:4]]
(e) of mighty works (Tr., _Syn._, §xci), δ. ποιεῖν, [[Mrk.6.5; 9.39|Mrk.6:5 9:39]]; pl., [[Mat.7.22|Mat.7:22]], [[Mrk.6.2|Mrk.6:2]], [[Luk.10.13|Luk.10:13]], al.; σημεῖακ. δ., [[Act.8.13|Act.8:13]] δ. κ. τέρατα κ. σημεῖα, [[Act.2.22|Act.2:22]], [[2Co.12.12|2Co.12:12]].
_SYN._: βία, ἐνέργεια, ἐξουσία, ἰσχύς, κράτος (see Tr., l.with; Cremer, 218, 236; _DB_, i, 616; iv, 29; _DCG_, i, 607; ii, 188). (AS)
